        "original_id": "17e7109a-9298-5ec9-ad9f-ba399dd5128e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rickard Rydell\n- Companies: Volvo Cars, Mitsubishi\n- Products: Volvo S40, Mitsubishi Carisma\n- Events: 1998 British Touring Car Championship\n- Places: Born, Netherlands\n- Organizations: NedCar factory\n\nFacts:\n- Volvo Cars marketed and produced the compact luxury car Volvo S40 from 1995 to 2012 across two generations.\n- During the time of the first-generation Volvo S40, Mitsubishi co-developed the Mitsubishi Carisma with Volvo.\n- The Mitsubishi Carisma shared its chassis with the first-generation Volvo S40.\n- The two companies co-owned the NedCar factory in Born, Netherlands, where the Mitsubishi Carisma was built.\n- Rickard Rydell won the 1998 British Touring Car Championship in a Volvo S40 with one round to spare.",
